{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>(She said) \"A vineyard was Solomon's\" [in בבעל המון she praises herself for the abundance of her love for her beloved, and the matter is that] Solomon the king gave his vineyard to keepers, and he took from the fruit of the vineyard [that the keepers brought him] a thousand silver, but I did not do so; rather, my vineyard (which is mine) is before me — I shall delight in it with you, and I do not want wealth [neither principal nor profit]. You, Solomon, take (from my) the fruit of your vineyard, and the keepers shall also take two hundred." "<b>The third time</b><br>\"A vineyard was Solomon's.\" Like the matter of \"For the vineyard of YHWH of Hosts is the house of Israel,\" and the matter is that Solomon ruled over all Israel [and this is the matter of בבעל המון, that all the multitude was his]." "\"He gave the vineyard to keepers.\" The matter is that he caused the kingdom to be divided, and he did not give to his sons in Jerusalem but two portions out of twelve, and they are Judah and Benjamin." "\"Each shall bring in its fruit a thousand silver.\" This is Jeroboam son of Nebat, who had ten portions."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "Bracketed material appears to be interpolated glosses within the manuscript tradition; translated as received."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:07.422973353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}